# qemu-bin/ -- the qemu binaries of the CI
#
# The qemu job of the CI (z_qemu_test_run.yml) and uc_devel take
# qemu-bin/<binary>.xz for the first word of the target's qemu command.
#
# The binaries are statically linked, so they run on any x86_64 Linux host,
# and carry the firmware they load (bios-256k.bin, OpenBIOS, OpenSBI,
# SeaBIOS-hppa, palcode-clipper, the efi NIC ROMs, the s3adsp1800 device
# tree): qemu_find_file() falls back to the built-in copy when a file is in
# none of the data directories, so no pc-bios or share/qemu directory is
# needed.  A directory given with -L still wins.
#
# All 38 come from the qemu fork lordrasmus/qemu, branch uclibc-ng, at
# 4e86befe6b (upstream qemu 71f25c7541, v11.1.0-3704, plus the fork), built
# together on the runner container:
#
#   ../configure --target-list=aarch64-softmmu,alpha-softmmu,arc-softmmu,\
#   arm-softmmu,avr32-softmmu,bfin-softmmu,c6x-softmmu,cris-softmmu,\
#   cskyv2-softmmu,frv-softmmu,h8300-softmmu,hppa-softmmu,i386-softmmu,\
#   ia64-softmmu,kvx-softmmu,lm32-softmmu,loongarch64-softmmu,m68k-softmmu,\
#   meta-softmmu,microblaze-softmmu,mips-softmmu,mips64-softmmu,\
#   mips64el-softmmu,mipsel-softmmu,nds32-softmmu,nios2-softmmu,or1k-softmmu,\
#   ppc-softmmu,riscv32-softmmu,riscv64-softmmu,sh4-softmmu,sh4eb-softmmu,\
#   sparc-softmmu,sparc64-softmmu,tilegx-softmmu,v850-softmmu,x86_64-softmmu,\
#   xtensa-softmmu --static --disable-gio \
#     --python=/opt/python3.12/bin/python3.12
#   make
#   strip qemu-system-*; xz -9 qemu-system-*
#
# The firmware is built in by default in the fork (--disable-embed-firmware
# leaves it out).  qemu-system-microblazeel is gone upstream (46a25ae3f0);
# the little-endian targets use qemu-system-microblaze
# -M petalogix-s3adsp1800,endianness=little.
#
# A single binary can still be replaced on its own when one machine changes;
# say here which fork commit it comes from.
#
# Replaced on their own since:
#   qemu-system-h8300  a77ea06d01 (on 4e86befe6b): LDC/STC Rn with register
#                      field 2 or 3 aborted qemu (helper_get_ccr assert)
#   qemu-system-meta   e70161431a (on a77ea06d01): a GET/SET without a valid
#                      base register crashed qemu in tcg_optimize instead of
#                      giving the guest SIGILL
